  "remTitle": "{topic, select, ramadan{🌙 Ramadan begins tonight}dhulHijjah{🕋 The best ten days begin}arafah{🤲 Tomorrow is the Day of Arafah}eidFitr{🎉 Eid al-Fitr is tomorrow}eidAdha{🐑 Eid al-Adha is tomorrow}tasua{🗓️ Fast Tasu'a tomorrow}ashura{🌊 Tomorrow is Ashura}whiteDays{🌕 The white days start tomorrow}monday{🗓️ Fast tomorrow, Monday}thursday{🗓️ Fast tomorrow, Thursday}jumuah{🕌 Jumu'ah Mubarak}fridayLastHour{🤲 The hour of Friday is here}suhoor{🌙 Time for suhoor}iftar{🌅 Time to break your fast}laylatAlQadr{✨ Tonight may be Laylat al-Qadr}morningAdhkar{☀️ Morning adhkar}eveningAdhkar{🌇 Evening adhkar}lastThird{🌌 The last third of the night}bedtime{😴 Before you sleep} other{}}",
  "remBody": "{topic, select, ramadan{Taraweeh tonight, suhoor before Fajr. Whoever fasts Ramadan with faith and hope of reward is forgiven his past sins (Bukhari).}dhulHijjah{No days are good deeds more beloved to Allah than these ten (Bukhari). Takbir, fasting, charity: tap to plan them.}arafah{Fasting it wipes out the sins of the past year and the coming one (Muslim). Make your intention tonight.}eidFitr{Give zakat al-fitr before the Eid prayer, and say the takbir from tonight. Tap for the Sunnah of Eid.}eidAdha{Say the takbir, pray Eid in the morning, then offer your sacrifice. Tap for the Sunnah of Eid.}tasua{The Prophet ﷺ meant to fast the 9th with Ashura (Muslim). Ashura comes the day after.}ashura{Fasting Ashura wipes out the sins of the past year (Muslim). Make your intention tonight.}whiteDays{Fast the 13th, 14th and 15th: three days a month is like fasting the whole year (Bukhari).}monday{Deeds are shown to Allah on Mondays and Thursdays, and the Prophet ﷺ loved to be fasting (Tirmidhi).}thursday{Deeds are shown to Allah on Mondays and Thursdays, and the Prophet ﷺ loved to be fasting (Tirmidhi).}jumuah{Ghusl, go early, read Surat al-Kahf and send many blessings on the Prophet ﷺ today.}fridayLastHour{There is an hour on Friday when every dua is answered (Bukhari). Seek it now, before Maghrib.}suhoor{Eat suhoor, for there is blessing in it (Bukhari). Fajr is coming soon.}iftar{People stay upon good as long as they hasten to break the fast (Bukhari). Make dua as you break it.}laylatAlQadr{Better than a thousand months (Qur'an 97:3). Pray, and say: Allahumma innaka ʿafuwwun tuhibbul-ʿafwa faʿfu ʿanni (Tirmidhi).}morningAdhkar{A few minutes of remembrance to begin your day under Allah's protection.}eveningAdhkar{The evening remembrance, before Maghrib. Tap to read it.}lastThird{Allah descends to the lowest heaven and asks: who is calling on Me, that I may answer him? (Bukhari)}bedtime{Ayat al-Kursi, the last two verses of al-Baqarah and the sleep dua. Two minutes.} other{}}",
  "remKind": "{kind, select, ramadan{Start of Ramadan}dhulHijjah{Dhul Hijjah and Arafah}eid{Eid}ashura{Tasu'a and Ashura}whiteDays{The white days}monThu{Monday and Thursday fasts}jumuah{Jumu'ah morning}fridayLastHour{The hour of Friday}suhoor{Suhoor}iftar{Iftar}laylatAlQadr{Odd nights of the last ten}morningAdhkar{Morning adhkar}eveningAdhkar{Evening adhkar}lastThird{The last third of the night}bedtime{Before sleep} other{}}",
  "remWhen": "{kind, select, ramadan{The night Ramadan begins}dhulHijjah{When the ten days begin, and the eve of Arafah}eid{The evening before each Eid}ashura{The evenings before the 9th and 10th of Muharram}whiteDays{The evening before the 13th, every month}monThu{Sunday and Wednesday evenings}jumuah{Friday morning}fridayLastHour{Friday, the last hour before Maghrib}suhoor{Before Fajr, every day of Ramadan}iftar{At Maghrib, every day of Ramadan}laylatAlQadr{Nights of the 21st, 23rd, 25th, 27th and 29th}morningAdhkar{After Fajr}eveningAdhkar{After Asr}lastThird{When the last third begins}bedtime{At your bedtime} other{}}",
